===== README.md =====
# Observer managed-settings for Claude Code

Each artifact has a DIFFERENT job:

- **allowed-mcp-server.json** is ONE `allowedMcpServers` entry,
  `{"serverCommand":["observer","serve"]}`, matching the MCP server `observer init` registers per node in
  `~/.claude.json` (no managed-mcp.json is generated, so developers keep
  their own servers). Add it to the `allowedMcpServers` list your
  managed settings already deploy; if they deploy none, deploy nothing:
  an `allowedMcpServers` list holding only this entry blocks every
  other MCP server. Claude Code matches it exactly, every argument in
  order, so it must equal the command on the nodes (check one with
  `claude mcp get observer`; regenerate with `--mcp-binary <path>` when
  init wrote an absolute path, or when it added `--config <file>`, and
  add that pair to the entry). An org-managed Linux or macOS node that
  opts in with `[observer.mcp] stable_command = true` (off until its live
  check passes) registers the bare `observer` whenever PATH runs that same
  install, so the default entry matches it. `observer doctor` reports a managed
  allowlist that refuses Observer's server.

- **managed-settings.json** (env block) points Claude Code's native OTel
  exporter at Observer's OTLP receiver (`http://127.0.0.1:4317`). **THIS** is what delivers
  telemetry. The receiver must be running (`[ingest.otel].enabled = true`)
  and reachable from each node.

- **managed-settings.json** (env block) also sets `ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8820`,
  routing Claude Code's traffic through that endpoint - either a node's
  Observer proxy (`http://127.0.0.1:8820` by default) or, in Gateway-Mode thin deployments, a
  direct org AI Gateway URL. Switching between the two is a pure base-URL
  swap: no other tool/MCP registration changes.

## Deploy

- **File channel (single node, no license):** write to
  `/etc/claude-code/managed-settings.json` (Linux/WSL). Verify with
  `/status` → expect `(file)`. On WSL, write inside the distro or set
  `wslInheritsWindowsSettings: true`.
- **Native Windows nodes:** write managed-settings.json to
  `C:\Program Files\ClaudeCode\managed-settings.json` (administrator-writable; the legacy
  `C:\ProgramData\ClaudeCode` path is not read).
- **Server channel (fleet):** upload the same payload in your
  Teams/Enterprise admin console's managed-settings section.
